# The images (Dockerfile) need the Go sources, the domains and the methodologies, nothing else:
# everything is left out, then only what the build reads is let in, so a local web/node_modules,
# .goap (workspaces, SQLite, the claude agent's npm install), bin/, binaries built at the root or a
# Rust target/ never reach the build context.
*

!go.work
!go.work.sum
!contracts/
!lib/
!graph/
!engine/
!mcp/
!gateway/
!platform/
!domains/
!methodologies/
# the Rust graph service and its proxy (ADR 0163): the workspace, the protos it generates from, without its build
!rust/
!proto/
rust/target/

# what go build never reads, inside the modules
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/
**/node_modules/
**/*.md
